amsung SDI006400.KS SNE Research FY2025; share down on premium-EV demand softness  | 2.7%\n10  | Sunwoda Electronic300207.SZ SNE Research FY2025  | 2.4%\n11  | Others REPT BATTERO, Farasis, AESC, Northvolt (in restructuring), and tail  | 10.9%\n\n## Batteries at a Glance\n\nEight sourced snapshot metrics. Pack price and chemistry mix are omitted here because they already have dedicated charts.\n\n2024 energy-sector battery demand\n\n1 TWh\n\nIEA: EV plus stationary storage demand hit 1 TWh in 2024. EV batteries were over 950 GWh, up 25% from 2023.\n\nIEA GEO 2025\n\nUS utility-scale storage, end-2025\n\n43.6 GW\n\nEIA Preliminary Monthly Electric Generator Inventory. Operators added another 8.3 GW in H1 2026, reaching nearly 52 GW.\n\nEIA\n\nCATL 2025 cell sales\n\n661 GWh\n\nCompany-reported lithium-ion sales: 541 GWh power batteries and 121 GWh energy-storage batteries.\n\nCATL 2025 AR\n\nSNE 2025 ESS cell shipments\n\n550 GWh\n\nGlobal energy-storage battery shipments, up 79% year on year, as cited in CATL's 2025 annual report from SNE Research.\n\nSNE via CATL AR\n\nSNE 2025 EV battery usage\n\n1,187 GWh\n\nGlobal power-battery usage volume, up 31.7% year on year, as cited in CATL's 2025 annual report from SNE Research.\n\nSNE via CATL AR\n\nTesla Energy 2025 deployments\n\n46.7 GWh\n\nSum of Tesla-reported quarterly energy storage deployments in 2025 (10.4 + 9.6 + 12.5 + 14.2 GWh), matching the 46.7 GWh full-year figure in Tesla's Q4 2025 deliveries release.\n\nTesla earnings\n\nWorld lithium mine output 2025\n\n290 kt\n\nUSGS estimate, lithium content, excluding withheld US production. Up 31% from 222 kt in 2024. Global consumption 263 kt.\n\nUSGS MCS 2026\n\nIEA 2030 NZE battery storage\n\n1,200 GW\n\nNet Zero Emissions by 2050 pathway. Batteries supply 90% of the sixfold rise in energy storage to 1,500 GW by 2030.\n\nIEA Batteries 2024\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n详情_CNESA 储能研究平台 (https://www.esresearch.c