product mix and supply chain traceability capabilities.’ Read more here.\n\nTop 10 Global EV Battery Suppliers\n\n### Top 10 Global EV Battery Suppliers\n\nRank  | Group  | 2025.1-7 (GWh)  | 2026.1-7 (GWh)  | YoY  | 2025 M/S  | 2026 M/S\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n1  | CATL  | 228.7  | 289.6  | +26.6%  | 38.0%  | 39.9%\n2  | BYD  | 101.9  | 106.7  | +4.7%  | 16.9%  | 14.7%\n3  | LG Energy Solution  | 57.8  | 60.3  | +4.5%  | 9.6%  | 8.3%\n4  | CALB  | 27.8  | 37.3  | +34.3%  | 4.6%  | 5.1%\n5  | Gotion  | 23.6  | 34.0  | +44.2%  | 3.9%  | 4.7%\n6  | Panasonic  | 24.3  | 26.2  | +7.6%  | 4.0%  | 3.6%\n7  | EVE  | 16.3  | 25.0  | +53.1%  | 2.7%  | 3.5%\n8  | SK on  | 24.7  | 22.3  | -9.8%  | 4.1%  | 3.1%\n9  | SVOLT  | 13.6  | 18.9  | +39.1%  | 2.3%  | 2.6%\n10  | REPT  | 7.7  | 16.9  | +118.5%  | 1.3%  | 2.3%\n | Others  | 75.8  | 88.1  | +16.2%  | 12.6%  | 12.1%\n | Total  | 602.2  | 725.2  | +20.4%  | 100.0%  | 100.0%\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n\nUnit: GWh\n\nSource: Global EV and Battery Monthly Tracker, August 2026, SNE Research\n\n### Like this:\n\nLike\n\n### Related\n\nTagged: Batteries CATL China Electric Vehicles EVs SNE Research--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGlobal Renewable Energy and Battery Industry Brief (https://www.thedexs.com/post/renewable-energy-and-batteries/)\nciteturn112search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \n### Vehicle battery usage by supplier\n\nEV, PHEV and HEV registered during the period; stationary storage is excluded. Total installed battery energy: 844.2 GWh. This is a vehicle-battery segment, not the entire renewable-energy industry.\n\n80 countries covered by SNE Research · Share of battery energy in registered EV, PHEV and HEV vehicles (%)\n\n[Button: Full screen]\n\nView the data table\n\nVehicle battery usage by supplier · January–August 2026 · Share of battery energy in registered EV, PHEV and HEV vehicles (%)\nSupplier  | Share\n--- | ---\nCATL  | 39.4%\nBYD  | 15.1%\nLG Energy Solution  | 8.1%\nCALB  | 5.3%\nGotion  | 4.9%\nOther suppliers  | 27.2%\n\nDownload data (CSV)\n\nOther suppliers = 100 − 39.4 − 15.1 − 8.1 − 5.3 − 4.9 = 27.2%; the five named suppliers total 72.8%. SNE publishes CATL plus BYD at 54.6%; its one-decimal company values sum to 54.5%. The reason is unverified. Company values are not renormalised. Other suppliers is the complement of the five shown, not the source table’s separate Others category.\n\nSource: SNE Research — Global EV and Battery Monthly Tracker — January to August 2026 (2026-10-02). Reviewed 2026-10-06.\n\nFigure 2. Supplier shares of battery energy in registered EV, PHEV and HEV vehicles, January–August 2026, 80 countries. Total: 844.2 GWh. Shares in percent. Other suppliers is a calculated residual; stationary storage is excluded. Source: SNE Research [M01].\n\nThese figures cannot establish a global utilisation rate: EV deployment is one application, whereas cell capacity serves a wider market. [G03] Author’s interpretation: a new factory announcement should be assessed against customer qualification, achievable output and intended applications. A large building and an expanding end market do not by themselves show that a particular production line will earn a return.\n\n### Vehicle battery competition within a defined market\n\nSNE Research’s release of 2 October 2026 estimates 844.2 GWh of battery energy in registered EV, PHEV and HEV vehicles across 80 countries from January to August 2026, up 19.7% year on year. Its supplier table places CATL at 39.4%, BYD at 15.1%, LG Energy Solution at 8.1%, CALB at 5.3% and Gotion at 4.9%. These are shares of that vehicle-battery usage measure, not of all renewable energy, all batteries or company revenue. [M01]\n\nThe chart uses the five published rounded supplier values. ‘Other suppliers’ is the calculated residual, 27.2%, covering every supplier outside those five. SNE separately publishes 54.6% for CATL plus BYD, while its one-decimal components sum to 54.5%; the exact reason is unverified. This review preserves the table’s precision and explains the discrepancy. It does not adjust the company values to force a different combined total. [M01]\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSNE Research: statistics and data (https://statorigin.org/sources/sne-research)\nciteturn112search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; \n\nPublisher · 1 documents · 4 figures\n\n# SNE Research\n\n4 verified figures from 1 publication by SNE Research, a research. Every figure links to the document and sentence it came from.\n\nCopy citation JSON Official site Cite and reuse\n\nData points\n\n4\n\nDocuments\n\n1\n\nIndicators\n\n4\n\nRegions\n\n1\n\nPublisher type\n\nResearch\n\n## Documents used\n\nEvery publication we have taken a number from, with the date we read it and the link status at that time.\n\nDocument  | Type  | Published  | Retrieved  | Link  | Data points\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFrom Jan to Nov 2024, Global EV Battery Usage Posted 785.6GWh, a 26.4% YoY Growth Public summary of a proprietary report  | Press release  | 6 Jan 2025  | 14 Sep 2026  | Reachable  | 4\n\n## Measures from this publisher\n\nEvery measure taken from SNE Research, with its latest value and trend. Each value opens its record.\n\n### Growth and change 1\n\nMeasure Latest Change Trend Source\n\nEV battery energy usage growth rate Global · January–November 2024 26.4% SNE Research 1 record\n\n### Other measures 3\n\nMeasure Latest Change Trend Source\n\nBYD EV battery energy usage Global · January–November 2024 134.4 GWh SNE Research 1 record\n\nCATL EV battery energy usage Global · January–November 2024 289.3 GWh SNE Research 1 record\n\nEV battery energy usage (SNE Research) Global · January–November 2024 785.6 GWh SNE Research 1 record\n\n4 measures. Each name opens the full series; each value opens the record with its source evidence.\n\n## Cite this page\n\nData on this page is published under CC BY 4.0. Credit SNE Research as the original publisher; each record page carries its own citation.\n\nSNE Research. Retrieved from StatOrigin: https://statorigin.org/sources/sne-research\n\nLast verified 27 September 2026. Link status is rechecked weekly.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGlobal EV battery market share in Jan-Feb 2025: CATL 38.2%, BYD 16.9% - CnEVPost (https://cnevpost.com/2025/04/08/global-ev-battery-market-share-jan-feb-2025/)\nciteturn112search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; \n\n# Global EV battery market share in Jan-Feb 2025: CATL 38.2%, BYD 16.9%\n\nLei Kang • Apr 8, 2025, 10:51 AM GMT+8\n\n>   * CATL and BYD's combined EV battery installed capacity in January-February was 71.5 GWh, accounting for 55.1 percent of the global total.\n>   * There are six Chinese companies in the top 10.\n\nCATL (SHE: 300750) and BYD (HKEX: 1211, OTCMKTS: BYDDY) remained the world's 2 largest electric vehicle (EV) battery makers in the first two months of this year.\n\nGlobal electric vehicle (EV) battery usage in January-February totaled 129.9 GWh, up 40.3 percent from 92.6 GWh in the same period last year, according to data released today by South Korean market researcher SNE Research.\n\nCATL installed 49.6 GWh of EV batteries in January-February, up 39.7 percent from 35.5 GWh in the same period a year ago.\n\nThe Chinese power battery giant continued to be the world's No. 1 battery supplier in January-February with a 38.2 percent share, and remained the only battery supplier in the world with a market share of more than 30 percent.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n中创新航：2026年中期净利润同比增长100.69% 拟每股派息0.06元 _ 东方财富网 (https://wap.eastmoney.com/a/202608303859442236.html)\nciteturn112search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; \n\n# 中创新航：2026年中期净利润同比增长100.69% 拟每股派息0.06元\n\n中国证券报·中证网 08-30 17:44 评论\n\n中证智能财讯中创新航（03931）8月28日披露2026年中期报告。报告期内，公司实现营业收入270.84亿元，同比增长64.96%；归母净利润9.35亿元，同比增长100.69%；据报告显示，中创新航基本每股收益为0.5276元，平均净资产收益率为2.57%。公司2026年中期分配预案为：每股派息0.06元人民币。\n\n以8月28日收盘价计算，中创新航目前市盈率（TTM）约14.37倍，市净率（TTM）约0.74倍，市销率（TTM）约0.5倍。\n\n\n2026年上半年，公司平均净资产收益率为2.57%，较上年同期上升1.24个百分点。\n\nImageImageImageImageImageImage\n\n资产重大变化方面，截至2026年上半年，公司存货较上期末增加79.13%，占公司总资产比重上升2.77个百分点；预付账款较上期末增加35.41%，占公司总资产比重上升1.05个百分点；应收票据及应收账款较上期末增加5.08%，占公司总资产比重下降0.77个百分点；固定资产较上期末增加12.61%，占公司总资产比重下降0.64个百分点。\n\n\n负债重大变化方面，截至2026年上半年，公司合同负债较上期末增加508.09%，占公司总资产比重上升0.96个百分点；短期借款较上期末增加19.76%，占公司总资产比重上升0.89个百分点；应付债券较上期末增加68.42%，占公司总资产比重上升0.61个百分点；其他应付款(含利息和股利)较上期末增加5.99%，占公司总资产比重下降0.32个百分点。\n\nImageImageImage\n\n2026年上半年，公司流动比率为0.78，速动比率为0.6。\n\n（文章来源：中国证券报·中证网）\n\n文章来源：中国证券报·中证网\n\n文章作者：孙萍\n\n原标题：中创新航：2026年中期净利润同比增长100.69% 拟每股派息0.06元\n\n郑重声明：东方财富发布此内容旨在传播更多信息，与本站立场无关，不构成投资建议。据此操作，风险自担。"
